    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21223" root="سوس" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاسٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُوسٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>A canker,</i> or <i>corrosion,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَادِحٌ</span>,) <i>in a tooth:</i> (AZ, K:) without and
without teshdeed. (AZ.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And A tooth <i>that
has been eaten,</i> or <i>corroded:</i> (L, K, * TA:) originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَائِسٌ</span>; like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَارٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَائِرٌ</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسُوسٌ</span>, in two places.

